  Note: in future versions of the protocol, this will be required.
- `meta::Union{Nothing,Dict{String,Any}}` (optional): The _meta property is reserved by ACP to allow clients and agents to attach additional
  metadata to their interactions. Implementations MUST NOT make assumptions about values at
  these keys.

  See protocol docs: [Extensibility](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/extensibility)
"""
struct InitializeRequest <: ProtocolObject
    json::Dict{String,Any}
end

"""
    ClientCapabilities(; fs = nothing, terminal = nothing, session = nothing, subagents = nothing, plan = nothing, auth = nothing, elicitation = nothing, nes = nothing, position_encodings = nothing, meta = nothing)

Capabilities supported by the client.

Advertised during initialization to inform the agent about
available features and methods.

See protocol docs: [Client Capabilities](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/initialization#client-capabilities)

# Fields

- `fs::FileSystemCapabilities` (optional): File system capabilities supported by the client.
  Determines which file operations the agent can request.
- `terminal::Bool` (optional): Whether the Client support all `terminal/*` methods.
- `session::Union{Nothing,ClientSessionCapabilities}` (optional): Session-related capabilities supported by the client.

  Optional. Omitted or `null` both mean the client does not advertise any
  session-related extensions.
- `subagents::Union{Nothing,SubagentCapabilities}` (optional): **UNSTABLE**

  This capability is not part of the spec yet, and may be removed or changed at any point.

  Whether the client understands exposed subagent sessions.

  Optional and nullable. Omitted or `null` both mean the client does not
  advertise support.
  Supplying `{}` means the client understands child associations, work-state
  snapshots, session-directed messages, and restricted-session semantics.
- `plan::Union{Nothing,PlanCapabilities}` (optional): **UNSTABLE**

  This capability is not part of the spec yet, and may be removed or changed at any point.

  Whether the client supports `plan_update` and `plan_removed` session updates.

  Optional. Omitted or `null` both mean the client does not advertise support.
  Supplying `{}` means the client can receive both update types.
- `auth::AuthCapabilities` (optional): Authentication capabilities supported by the client.
  Determines which authentication method types the agent may include
  in its `InitializeResponse`.
- `elicitation::Union{Nothing,ElicitationCapabilities}` (optional): Elicitation capabilities supported by the client.
  Determines which elicitation modes the agent may use.

  Optional. Omitted or `null` both mean the client does not advertise
  elicitation support.
- `nes::Union{Nothing,ClientNesCapabilities}` (optional): **UNSTABLE**

  This capability is not part of the spec yet, and may be removed or changed at any point.

  NES (Next Edit Suggestions) capabilities supported by the client.

  Optional. Omitted or `null` both mean the client does not advertise any
  NES suggestion-kind extensions.
- `position_encodings::Vector{PositionEncodingKind}` (optional): **UNSTABLE**

  This capability is not part of the spec yet, and may be removed or changed at any point.

  The position encodings supported by the client, in order of preference.
- `meta::Union{Nothing,Dict{String,Any}}` (optional): The _meta property is reserved by ACP to allow clients and agents to attach additional
  metadata to their interactions. Implementations MUST NOT make assumptions about values at
  these keys.

  See protocol docs: [Extensibility](https://agentclientprotocol.com/protocol/extensibility)
"""
struct ClientCapabilities <: ProtocolObject
    json::Dict{String,Any}
end

